From bcf0bb6822062952174bc0ab61c81ede74a37b02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:45:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 19/47] vrend: require EXT_texture_shadow_lod only for a real
 bias or LOD

TGSI appends every operand that does not fit the coordinate vector to the
same buffer the emitter uses for a LOD bias, so several lookups look biased
although nothing about them is: TGSI_OPCODE_TG4, where the slot holds the
gather's comparison value or its component, TGSI_OPCODE_TEX2 on
TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY, where it holds the lookup's comparison value,
and TGSI_OPCODE_TXD, where it holds the two gradients. All three asked the
host for EXT_texture_shadow_lod.

The extension exists to add the bias and explicit-LOD forms that core leaves
out for these shadow samplers, which is what TXB, TXL, TXB2 and TXL2 really
pass; textureGather on a shadow sampler, texture(samplerCubeArrayShadow,
vec4, float) and textureGrad on sampler2DArrayShadow or samplerCubeShadow are
core GLSL and core ESSL. A desktop GL host has no reason to implement the
extension - zink never sets pipe_caps::texture_shadow_lod, so Mesa's GLSL
compiler rejects the `require` outright - and the generated shader then fails
to compile. For the gather that put the context into error, which on this
host costs the rest of the run rather than the one draw; for the other forms
the draw is dropped and the guest reads back the surface as it stands. That
is what all three shader stages of dEQP-GL45-ES31.functional.shaders.
opaque_type_indexing.sampler.*.samplercubearrayshadow report, and what
dEQP-GLES3.functional.shaders.texture_functions.texturegrad.
sampler2darrayshadow_{vertex,fragment} report as a wholly wrong image
(difference 3677.94 against a threshold of 0.07). The generated lookup is
already correct - `textureGrad(vssamp0, in_1, in_2.xy, in_3.xy)` for
`TXD OUT[1].x, IN[1], IN[2].xyyy, IN[3].xyyy, SAMP[0], SHADOW2D_ARRAY` - and
only the extension line is rejected: "0:2(12): error: extension
`GL_EXT_texture_shadow_lod' unsupported in vertex shader", after which the
context fails to dispatch DRAW_VBO.

Ask for the extension from the four opcodes that pass a bias or an explicit
LOD instead of naming the ones that do not, so a later operand in that buffer
cannot reintroduce the same mistake. The GLES-only requirement that covers
the textureOffset forms core ESSL leaves out follows the same rule and keeps
its offset case, except for TXD: textureGradOffset on sampler2DArrayShadow is
core ESSL as well. A host that does advertise the extension is unaffected,
because the requirement was never what made any of these forms work: the
generated call is the same either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_shader.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
index 83f8bad..5d9d12f 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -3366,15 +3366,36 @@ static void translate_tex(struct dump_ctx *ctx,
 
    bool has_bias = strbuf_get_len (&bias_buf) != 0;
    bool has_offset = strbuf_get_len (&offset_buf) != 0;
-   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias
-   if (has_bias &&
+   // Every operand that does not fit the coordinate vector is appended to the
+   // same buffer a LOD bias uses, so several lookups look biased although
+   // nothing about them is. EXT_texture_shadow_lod only adds the bias and
+   // explicit-LOD forms that core leaves out for these shadow samplers, so
+   // only the opcodes that really pass one may ask for it: TXB and TXL append
+   // a bias or LOD, TXB2 and TXL2 append one after the comparison value. TEX2
+   // appends a comparison value alone, TG4 a comparison value or a gather
+   // component, and TXD two gradients; texture(samplerCubeArrayShadow, vec4,
+   // float), textureGather on a shadow sampler and textureGrad on
+   // sampler2DArrayShadow or samplerCubeShadow are all core GLSL and core
+   // ESSL. Requiring the extension for them fails to compile on a host that
+   // has no reason to implement it.
+   const bool lookup_passes_lod =
+      inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXB ||
+      inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXL ||
+      inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXB2 ||
+      inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXL2;
+
+   if (has_bias && lookup_passes_lod &&
        (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY))
       ctx->shader_req_bits |= SHADER_REQ_TEXTURE_SHADOW_LOD;
 
-   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod also adds the missing textureOffset for 2DArrayShadow in GLES
-   if ((has_bias || has_offset) && ctx->cfg->use_gles &&
+   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod also adds the missing textureOffset for
+   // 2DArrayShadow in GLES, but not textureGradOffset, which is core there
+   // too.
+   if (ctx->cfg->use_gles &&
+       ((has_bias && lookup_passes_lod) ||
+        (has_offset && inst->Instruction.Opcode != TGSI_OPCODE_TXD)) &&
        (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW1D_ARRAY ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY))
       ctx->shader_req_bits |= SHADER_REQ_TEXTURE_SHADOW_LOD;
